From d084e2fdb422a4929c3acd0474a14ae94e112d85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: User <user@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:12:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(security): server identity challenge, CSP fallback,
 and hardening

Close the local port-hijack chain: the server now writes a 0600 identity
token when orchestrated by Electron and answers a timingSafeEqual challenge
on GET /api/identity (404 otherwise); Electron probes health, watchdog, and
Dock reuse through that challenge, gates all IPC behind a verified flag,
and no longer trusts any responder on the port. Add a meta CSP fallback to
index.html for server-bypass scenarios, sweep orphan .temp-export backups
at startup, and validate world.ts route payloads with zod up front so
malformed input fails before quota reservation (existing error contracts
unchanged).
